  {
   "n": 2,
   "type": "MSQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "multi | Marks +2",
   "html": "<p>Select the incorrect statement(s) from the given below options.<br>A buffalo is tied with a pole of 200 m long rope. At some point of time,</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>the probability that the buffalo is at least 50 m away from the pole is 1/4</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>the probability that the buffalo is within the distance of 40 m of the pole is 1/5</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>the probability that buffalo is at least 100 m away from the pole is 1/2</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>the probability that the buffalo is atmost 150 m from the pole is 3/4</p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "C",
    "D"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "B, A, D, C",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0
   },
   "solution": "<p>The buffalo can be anywhere within the circular area defined by the length of the rope (<em>R </em>= 200 m).<br>Let &lsquo;<em>x</em>&rsquo; denote the distance of the buffalo from the pole. The probability that the buffalo is within&nbsp;a certain distance &lsquo;<em>r</em>&rsquo; from the pole is proportional to the area of the circle with radius '<em>r</em>' divided&nbsp;by the total area of the circle with radius &lsquo;<em>r</em>&rsquo; i.e.</p>\n<p><img src=\"media/e2/e2f949582ad25b560a7e.png\"></p>\n<p><img src=\"media/f7/f71b54cc0a631559020d.png\"></p>"
  },
