  {
   "n": 13,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "single | Marks +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>How many 3-digit numbers can be formed using three distinct single digit prime numbers?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>64</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>24</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>12</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>4</p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "B"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "B",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>The set of single-digit prime numbers is {2, 3, 5, 7}.<br>The number of ways to select 3 digits out of 4 is 4.<br>The number of ways to arrange them to form a 3-digit number = 3! = 6<br>Total possible 3 digit numbers = Number of ways to select &times; Ways to arrange<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; = 4 &times; 6 = 24</p>"
  },
